From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nds-ports <nds-ports@localhost>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 07:09:59 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Parse text without scanf and strtod

Savegames, their comments for the menu and point files are read a word
at a time with COM_ReadWord and Q_atof instead of fscanf, entity fields
with Q_atof instead of atof. The C library's scanf and strtod, with
their wide character tables, take more room than all of Quake's menus.
---
 WinQuake/common.c   | 22 ++++++++++++++++++++++
 WinQuake/common.h   |  1 +
 WinQuake/host_cmd.c | 14 +++++++-------
 WinQuake/menu.c     |  5 ++---
 WinQuake/pr_edict.c |  4 ++--
 WinQuake/r_part.c   |  3 ++-
 6 files changed, 36 insertions(+), 13 deletions(-)

diff --git a/WinQuake/common.c b/WinQuake/common.c
index 6da0f96..c1927ae 100644
--- a/WinQuake/common.c
+++ b/WinQuake/common.c
@@ -901,6 +901,28 @@ void COM_DefaultExtension (char *path, char *extension)
 }
 
 
+/*
+==============
+COM_ReadWord
+
+Reads the next word of a text file, like the %s of fscanf, the word is
+empty at the end of the file
+==============
+*/
+char *COM_ReadWord (FILE *f, char *word, int size)
+{
+	int		c, len;
+
+	do
+		c = fgetc (f);
+	while (c != EOF && c <= ' ');
+	for (len = 0 ; c != EOF && c > ' ' ; c = fgetc (f))
+		if (len < size - 1)
+			word[len++] = c;
+	word[len] = 0;
+	return word;
+}
+
 /*
 ==============
 COM_Parse
